cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "jev-tune: System-1 typed decisions for PID autotuning"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Jiawei"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lijiawei255/jev-tune"
url: "https://github.com/lijiawei255/jev-tune"
abstract: >-
  A CPU-only PID autotuner in which each decision is a Jev-style typed decision
  (choice / score / noul) produced by a 200 KB numeric head in 0.19 ms, instead
  of an autoregressive language-model call. Ships a Python simulator, a Simulink
  bridge that runs the head inside MATLAB, an MCP server, and benchmarks against
  Ziegler-Nichols, relay autotuning, CMA-ES, Bayesian optimisation and MATLAB
  pidtune.
keywords:
  - PID tuning
  - system identification
  - Simulink
  - control engineering
  - decision model
  - Jev
  - onnx
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
